# The repo is code + labels only. Everything a script can re-download or
# recompute stays out — together it is ~3 GB, which GitHub will not take and
# nobody wants in a clone. SETUP.md has the command that regenerates each item.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environment
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
myenv/
mynenv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / frontend
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
#
# Nothing here needs a token today — all four models are public — but an
# ignored .env now is cheaper than a leaked one later.
#
# .env.example is ignored too, and deliberately not exempted. It once held a
# real GROQ_API_KEY, which is exactly how template files leak: they look inert,
# so nobody checks them before committing. SETUP.md spells out the two lines
# the file would have contained.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FastF1 race cache          regenerate: python scripts/cache_sessions.py
#
# ~550 MB of parsed session data plus fastf1_http_cache.sqlite, FastF1's own
# request cache. Both are pure download artifacts keyed on race identity, so a
# fresh machine rebuilds them byte-for-byte.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/cache/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Radio audio               regenerate: python scripts/fetch_radio.py
#
# 446 mp3s, ~86 MB, fetched from the F1 live-timing service.
#
# index.csv is the exception and is COMMITTED below: it carries the `label`
# column, which is hand annotation and the one thing in data/ that no script
# can reproduce. Losing it means re-listening to 446 clips.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/clips/*
!data/clips/index.csv

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis cache            regenerate: python scripts/batch_analyse.py
#
# Now committed, reversing the earlier decision to ignore it. 853 files, 3.3 MB.
#
# The reason is the same one cache_sessions.py opens with: the demo must not
# depend on anything being reachable or on a long build step. Regenerating this
# takes ~20 minutes of local inference over 855 clips and needs every mp3 on
# disk, so a fresh clone without it shows an empty dashboard. At 3.3 MB that is
# a bad trade.
#
# data/clips/*.mp3 stays ignored — 170 MB of audio is a different question, and
# scripts/fetch_radio.py pulls it in a couple of minutes.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/results/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fusion training artifacts  regenerate: python scripts/fit_fusion.py
#
# features.json is a per-clip inference cache (STT + SER + text over every
# labelled clip) — large, and meaningless without the mp3s that produced it.
#
# fusion_head.json and driver_baselines.json are deliberately NOT ignored.
# They are a few KB, and rebuilding them needs the full clip set plus a model
# pass over it — so committing them is what lets a fresh clone run the demo
# with a trained head instead of falling back to population priors.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/labels/features.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local agent / tooling config — not part of the project
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hackathon handout material
#
# Organiser-supplied docs, not our work and not code. Kept local so the public
# repo carries only what we wrote.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.docx
*.pdf

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs / scratch
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
tmp/
scratch/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal documentation / planning files
#
# Development documentation not meant for public repo:
# - Planning documents
# - Status reports
# - Test reports
# - Architecture notes
# - Design documentation
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLAN.md
STATUS.md
TEST_REPORT.md
understand.md
CRITICAL_TECHNICAL_AUDIT.md
FRONTEND_REDESIGN.md
GLASSMORPHISM_REDESIGN.md
